</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Cross-dataset Generalization</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experimental setup.</span> In the cross-dataset generalization setting the classes from ImageNet are split among the clients for training, in a disjoint manner, and the resulting network is evaluated on 10 held out datasets not seen during training. In other words, it is a combination of the base-to-new generalization and the DG settings as it requires generalization to both unseen classes and data distributions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Main results.</span> The proposed setting poses a unique challenge, as the model should generalize to considerably different datasets. In Table. <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 4.2 Domain Generalization ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ FedMVP: Federated Multi-modal Visual Prompt Tuning for Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> we report the results of the cross-dataset generalization setting. We find the results to be consistent with the previous findings, where our proposed FedMVP generalizes to unseen classes and data distributions, outperforming all the text-based and multimodal-based prompting techniques on average. However, with FedMVP we notice a drop in performance with respect to the ZS-CLIP baseline for some fine-grained datasets, such as OxfordPets and StanfordCars, which is potentially due to overlapping attributes for visually similar categories.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Ablation Study</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation of proposed components in FedMVP.</span> In Table <a href="#S4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 4.4 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ FedMVP: Federated Multi-modal Visual Prompt Tuning for Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> we report the results of the ablation analysis on the base-to-new and MSST DG settings, where we meticulously test the performance gain obtained by adding one component of FedMVP at a time. We observe that each component brings non-negligible improvements over ZS-CLIP. For instance, the PromptFormer <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> plays a significant role by injecting textual information into the visual modality, thereby enhancing the semantic alignment between the two modalities. In addition, <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>con</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{con}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ 3.3.2 Training of FedMVP ‣ 3.3 Federated Multimodal Visual Prompt Tuning ‣ 3 Method ‣ FedMVP: Federated Multi-modal Visual Prompt Tuning for Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> helps to maintain smoothness in the learning process by ensuring consistency between the original and soft-augmented visual features, and slightly tuning LoRA parameters regularizes the model towards more stablity and less prone to overfitting.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="S4.T6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation on the FedMVP components.<span id="S4.T6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We report numbers for the base-to-new and MMST DG (on DomainBed) settings.</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="S4.T6.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:145.6pt;height:51.9pt;vertical-align:-24.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-31.2pt,11.1pt) scale(0.7,0.7) ;">
<table id="S4.T6.6.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T6.6.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
